    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nEntering cmdline with `:` when autocmd `pattern = { \":\", \"?\" }` calls the callback twice. Entering with `?` works as expected. \n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/856cbb72-12c8-44a3-97bd-201da2b92b26\n\nI tested other pattern combinations by hand and only found this problem with `:` + `?`\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. create this `init.lua`\n\n```lua\nlocal x = 0\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"CmdlineEnter\", {\n  group = vim.api.nvim_create_augroup(\"test-cmdline-enter\", {}),\n  pattern = { \":\", \"?\" },\n  callback = function(ev)\n    x = x + 1\n    vim.print(\"x=\" .. x, ev)\n  end\n})\n```\n\n2. `nvim --clean -u init.lua`. Enter the cmdline and observe callback firing twice.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nautocmd should only fire once when pressing `:`\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev+1049-ad3720b882\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nnot sure\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora 43 Linux 7.1.5-100.fc43.x86_64\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.44.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\ndnf install from copr agriffis/neovim-nightly",
